    "summary": "High‑energy Boulder marathon with monster Other One and China>Rider",
    "blurb": "The show delivers monster jams, notably The Other One and a smoking China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider, plus an explosive Not Fade Away/Going Down the Road medley in the third set. Jerry’s tiger‑guitar tone drives the band while Phil’s bass anchors the high‑energy improvisations. Soundboard recordings capture the rain‑soaked ambience and crystal‑clear second half.",
    "review": "September 3, 1972 at Folsom Field finds the Dead riding a literal storm into one of their most ferocious three‑set marathons. After a rain‑splattered opening that shifts from audience murk to pristine soundboard clarity, the band launches into a blistering The Other One where Jerry’s “tiger guitar” prowls over Phil’s thunderous bass, then rolls straight into a smoking China Cat Sunflower → I Know You Rider that feels like a brass‑blown sunrise after the downpour. The second set builds momentum with tight Playing In The Band and a seamless He's Gone → Other One transition before Wharf Rat caps the arc. The third set erupts with an unbridled Not Fade Away > Goin' Down The Road Feeling Bad > Not Fade Away medley, Johnny B. Goode’s rock‑n‑roll charge, and a soaring Bird Song that showcases the band’s collective groove. While the early audience sections are rough, the later soundboard feed preserves every nuance of the improvisations, making this show a must‑listen for anyone chasing high‑energy 1972 Dead.",
